{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy","id":1151253,"title":"Questions about Union Policy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-20T02:50:41-07:00","id":1151253,"title":"Questions about Union Policy","content":"1. Why the Union does not simply kidnap, clone and replace important figures such as presidents and prime ministers? <br /> <br /> 2. Why the Union does not wage total war against vampires?<br /> <br /> 3. Why the Union does not send its army to global hot zones in guise of government interference? <br /> <br /> 4. Does the Union capture and brainwash night-folk other than Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T07:51:11-07:00","id":1151316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why the Union does not simply kidnap, clone and replace important figures such as presidents and prime ministers? </div> </div> </div>In the old days they did, nowdays they do not do this. It's a policy about &quot;sleepers controling the world&quot;. More to the point, however, it was ludicrous and unnecessary: Technocrats made the modern world, Democracy was tested in a Horizon Realm before released to the masses and tested against other forms of political power. Why would them compromise their own social experiment?. If they NEED to change president they can do that, they're always close to the president, but that would imply that the president it's doing something that goes against Technocratic agenda, and that shouldn't happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why the Union does not wage total war against vampires? </div> </div> </div>Because vampires are something that's going to solve itself when Technocracy controls the Consensus because Consensus it's Reality. Or so most mages believe, why would the strategy that worked so well against dragons fail against vampires?. Vampires hidde themselves, and because of that they're contributing to their own eventual extermination in the minds of Technocrats. Technocrats may be wrong about this but they don't know better. Priority 1\u00ba it's to control the Consensus, priority 2\u00ba it's tying loose ends<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why the Union does not send its army to global hot zones in guise of government interference? </div> </div> </div>They totally do, it's just that they send it against magical treaths. Mind you, if they NEED to send an army to global cold zones they totally can, it's just harder to hide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the Union capture and brainwash night-folk other than Mage? </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. It's certainly possible and there is data about captured night-folk (including xenotransplants), but Mage doesn't deal much with the other Splats and so you don't see the &quot;dangerous cyberwolf opperative&quot; that believes Control it's Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T10:52:40-07:00","id":1151390,"title":"","content":"How involved other Splats are with the Technocracy is a sliding scale. You can go one extreme and say that the Vamps are so good at hiding that even the top top members of the Technocracy isn't aware of them, that werewolves are seen as no different from other spirits and thus something for the Engineers to focus on, and there is no real reason for a Technocrat to ever encounter a Wraith or a Fae, and thus it is never encountered.<br /> <br /> You can instead go the other extreme and the Syndicate working arm in arm with Pentex or even employing a large number of Glass Walkers. Making deals with a number of old generation Vamps in order to assist in covering up any evidence in exchange for information and other services. A number of high officials already making arangements with certain groups in Stygia to keep an eye on areas where the veil is weak.<br /> The official word may be that such creature simply do not exist, but all of this is on a need to know basis.<br /> <br /> How rampant this is would be up to you. The Union is many layered and often shrouded in bureaucratic secrecy. Not only does the right hand not know what the left hand is doing, but the thumb can't keep track of the fingers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T18:44:48-07:00","id":1152087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy#post1151253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Why the Union does not simply kidnap, clone and replace important figures such as presidents and prime ministers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Union knows that whatever utility could be derived from that plan doesn't outweigh the risk of discovery when the switch is made. The leaders of major countries especially are heavily observed public figures. The President of the United States is surrounded by aides, cabinet officials, and Secret Service guards at all times.<br /> <br /> The amount of work and resources the Union would need to use to make the switch without being discovered rises to levels that make it not worth the effort. Assuming they even could without being discovered. Remember, also, that many government heads in the modern world are elected officials, who'll leave office in a few short years anyway. Why bother go to the expense? Especially since sudden policy changes will attract attention? The Technocracy is far better off controlling the apparatus of government from the shadows, rather than trying to fully dominate individuals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Why the Union does not wage total war against vampires? </div> </div> </div>Why would they? As far as the Union knows, Vampires are a vanishing minority that will, in time, either die out or be mopped up easily later, when the Union has created its utopia. Moreover, Vampires are &quot;model Reality Deviants&quot;, who stay on their best behavior and police themselves. They have just as much - if not more - a vested interest in maintaining the Consensus as the Technocracy does. Simply put, while their...dietary requirements may be unsavory, and their powers may be quite Deviant, they are ultimately a low priority for the Union. As far as the Technocracy is concerned, it's a problem that can be placed on the back burner until all the more pressing concerns are dealt with. Concerns like the Traditions, who actively work against the vision of Reality the Union seeks to foster.<br /> <br /> Granted, also, the Vampires are excellent at hiding. The Union, for as good as they claim its surveillance network is, doesn't really know how many Vampires are running around. If they did have an accurate view of their numbers - and if they did know how close this &quot;Masquerade&quot; has come to falling - the Union might take the threat more seriously. But they don't, because they are working with incomplete information. It's the same reason why the Technocracy doesn't wage war against Pentex: it isn't aware just how thoroughly that corporation has been infested and dominated by a hostile alien presence, bent on the world's destruction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Why the Union does not send its army to global hot zones in guise of government interference? </div> </div> </div>The public tends to be critical of government interference as a matter of course. If the Union arranges for this sort of thing to happen - in and of itself not a trivial matter, getting governments to involve themselves when and where you want them - it attracts public attention to that same area. More attention, indeed, because supernatural groups (like, for instance, the Taftani) know enough about how the Union operates to see any such governmental interference as a potential Technocrat smokescreen. So while the public forces of government might cover the Union against the public (another big assumption), the ones they will often fight against see it as the smoke that signals fire. Instead of masking their presence, the Union may very well have tipped their enemies off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Does the Union capture and brainwash night-folk other than Mage? </div> </div> </div>Seems like more trouble than it's worth. Especially since supernatural creatures - like werewolves and vampires - will often have strong wills, making it harder to pull off.<br /> <br /> And, again, the Union underestimates how heavily the world is infested with Reality Deviants. To them, lycanthropes and hemovores are endangered species, on their way out. While there might be some utility to be wrought from turning them into agents, I would say it costs more time and resources than is worth it. Especially since they have legions of Extraordinary Citizens willing to undergo cybernetic or genetic modification, if the Union wanted empowered agents. Even if a vampire or werewolf is more powerful than five unAwakened mortals with Enhancements, those five mortals are far more willing to work with the Union, and can be distributed more flexibly than the single night-folk.<br /> <br /> Hell, &quot;more powerful than five mortals&quot; is an academic assumption, not taking into account that the five mortals have the advantage of numbers. Simply have a greater action economy puts the night-folk on the back foot; even if the Vampire uses Celerity or the Werewolf Rages, they'll at best have as many actions a round as the five mortals, and then not continually. And that further assumes the mortals don't have Enhancements that give them more actions.<br /> <br /> To avoid getting us bogged down in discussions of mechanics and edge cases, this is the sort of ballpark we're looking at. Where the Union will likely get just about as much value from using their own methods to make better agents and weapons, and at much less cost or hassle than if they tried to brainwash other night-folk to their cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T23:20:19-07:00","id":1152121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy#post1151253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Why the Union does not send its army to global hot zones in guise of government interference?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that the Technocracy has an army. They can and they do send Amalgams and Sympathizers to hot zones to accomplish various aims; Technocrats and Technocracy's agents placed in a military's chain of command can also help accomplish the Technocracy's goals in regards to a place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T07:11:36-07:00","id":1152184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like more trouble than it's worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another reason I can imagine, albeit it may sound weird, would be because of their ideology. <br /> <br /> Technocrats don't just abduct mages, they force the mages to adopt the new, correct, Paradigm. NWO even sees this as a kind of mercy, the other option would be to kill them...Vampires and others can't be &quot;converted to the right Paradigm&quot;, their powers are static. They don't choose to be deviants, they are a walking deviance. Vampires won't overcome their beast and it's urges with simple magick, and so, until they can be cured (from being a vampire), they will always be &quot;wrong&quot; for the Technocratical standard. While vampires may be able to operate under Static Reality, they don't operate the way Technocrats would want them to, and thus they can never be a part of the Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T19:29:11-07:00","id":1155917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1151316#post1151316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because vampires are something that's going to solve itself when Technocracy controls the Consensus because Consensus it's Reality. Or so most mages believe, why would the strategy that worked so well against dragons fail against vampires?. Vampires hidde themselves, and because of that they're contributing to their own eventual extermination in the minds of Technocrats. Technocrats may be wrong about this but they don't know better. Priority 1\u00ba it's to control the Consensus, priority 2\u00ba it's tying loose ends.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1152087#post1152087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they? As far as the Union knows, Vampires are a vanishing minority that will, in time, either die out or be mopped up easily later, when the Union has created its utopia. Moreover, Vampires are &quot;model Reality Deviants&quot;, who stay on their best behavior and police themselves. They have just as much - if not more - a vested interest in maintaining the Consensus as the Technocracy does. Simply put, while their...dietary requirements may be unsavory, and their powers may be quite Deviant, they are ultimately a low priority for the Union. As far as the Technocracy is concerned, it's a problem that can be placed on the back burner until all the more pressing concerns are dealt with. Concerns like the Traditions, who actively work against the vision of Reality the Union seeks to foster.<br /> <br /> Granted, also, the Vampires are excellent at hiding. The Union, for as good as they claim its surveillance network is, doesn't really know how many Vampires are running around. If they did have an accurate view of their numbers - and if they did know how close this &quot;Masquerade&quot; has come to falling - the Union might take the threat more seriously. But they don't, because they are working with incomplete information. It's the same reason why the Technocracy doesn't wage war against Pentex: it isn't aware just how thoroughly that corporation has been infested and dominated by a hostile alien presence, bent on the world's destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Camarilla is the single existing Vampire faction, that would be true.<br /> <br /> But there is Sabbat, the most monstrous of monsters. And both Sets are clearly present and kicking around in MtA.<br /> <br /> How the Union could ignore the Sabbat and its flagrant, egregious dismissal of Consensus and the Masses? They are certainly aware of its existence and activities. And Union is doubtlessly active in the Sabbat-controlled cities and countries. Why the Union does not conduct drone strike against areas of Southern America slums or bathe it with quasi-sunlight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-04-2017, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T20:15:34-07:00","id":1155926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1155917#post1155917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If Camarilla is the single existing Vampire faction, that would be true.<br /> <br /> But there is Sabbat, the most monstrous of monsters. And both Sets are clearly present and kicking around in MtA.<br /> <br /> How the Union could ignore the Sabbat and its flagrant, egregious dismissal of Consensus and the Masses? They are certainly aware of its existence and activities. And Union is doubtlessly active in the Sabbat-controlled cities and countries. Why the Union does not conduct drone strike against areas of Southern America slums or bathe it with quasi-sunlight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why doesn't the Technocracy engage in drone strikes against South American population centers?<br /> <br /> Gee, I don't know. It can't be because that would cause massive international incidents that couldn't be hidden if you tried. Because obviously the Technocracy is completely omnipotent and capable of perfectly hiding everything.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, while the Sabbat is looser with the Masquerade, they still grudgingly protect it (if only because they know they aren't strong enough (yet) to overthrow mortal society and put the kine in their proper place). Much as the sect mocks the Camarilla for its fixation on appearing human, the Sabbat know that true predators don't want their prey knowing they're there. Which means covering up supernatural stuff.<br /> <br /> Granted, the Sabbat version of a cover-up involves plenty of murder, but it gets the job done. Barely. So long as things don't look supernatural, neither the Sabbat nor the Technocracy care much about what the Sabbat does. If a few dozen bodies or thousands in property damage get dropped on a city from time to time, that's fine. Societal disfunction is, sadly, well within the Consensus.<br /> <br /> There's also entire factions within the Sabbat - like the Lasombra Kings and Queens of Night - that are devoted to dealing with the mortals. And that means somewhere, a beleagered Lasombra neonate is running himself ragged plugging holes in the Masquerade, paying off (or blackmailing or dominating) witnesses and authority figures, and generally keeping things this side of the line between order and complete madness.<br /> <br /> One last thing to consider: the Sabbat isn't a cohesive hierarchy, but a series of loosely connected cells. Any given pack is unlikely to know much about most other packs in the world. While this blunts their ability to organize, it also means that for every pack that gets caught, ten more go under the radar. For each one that attracts the Union's attention, ten more engage in atrocity while also keeping a lid on them (at least from a supernatural standpoint).<br /> <br /> So here's a question: why are you assuming the Union is even aware that the Sabbat is a whole sect at all, rather than a series of isolated groups that arise every so often? Vampires don't volunteer information about their kind or their political affiliations. For all the Union knows, getting together and forming packs is some kind of natural inclination for hemovores. Maybe signifying a different, more feral species to the largely solitary variety that likes to pretend to be human in order to blend in. And since these packs of hemovores seem to clean up after themselves (after a fashion), the occasional indiscretion isn't as much to worry about. Even these feral leeches seem to understand the value of hiding what they are, thereby contributing to the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Naturally, this assumes that the Union is ignorant of the full extent of the problem, or what the Tzimisce do behind closed doors (and how often they do it). If the Union had the sort of perfect knowledge of the Sabbat that we readers do, they'd see the sect as a much greater threat than it already is. But the World of Darkness is a place founded on ignorance - a place where every conspiracy keeps its cards close to its chest - and so the Union does not have perfect knowledge. All they can tell is that deranged hemovores sometimes get into groups and cause mayhem. The Sabbat's scattered, loose confederation ironically works in its favor when it comes to the Union, who won't as readily see the forest for the trees, and thus underestimates the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T21:05:08-07:00","id":1155936,"title":"","content":"NWO, the designated leader of the Union, <i>know </i>there are Camarilla, Sabbat and other Sects of Vampires, feed information to relevant parties, keep tabs one them and clearly <i>spying </i>them 24/7 through whatever means(I imagine captured, Processed and Conditioned Vampire sleeper agents), and very likely possess Book of Nod. That much is explicitly stated in their CB.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rumormongering among the vampires of an end of days, of a time when their legends rise up, has come and passed without incident. To be honest, that comes as a bit of a surprise, as the Statisticians calculated catastrophe in line with their prophecies. There is no open hostility between vampires and the Technocracy. They are content to keep to their \u201cMasquerade,\u201d and we are content to let them. Given our manpower issues, we\u2019re thankful not to have to police two different groups of Reality Deviants that wish to work in the open. Recently, the Collegia have settled the matter of Clan Tremere, vampires who work some form of blood magic. While there is still debate over theory regarding why their magic does not violate the stability of reality (most likely due to humanity\u2019s latent belief in vampires, reinforced by the surge of vampires in popular media), the fact that it doesn\u2019t makes the debate over reasons a moot point. As a threat, they have been downgraded as not worth the additional manpower, since they respect the Masquerade and do not risk Sleeper exposure. The Sabbat \u2014 a faction of vampires that does not concern itself with secrecy \u2014 is a potential thorn in our side, however. For now, the Sabbat vampires\u2019 struggle with the other vampire factions is a self-policing measure with which we\u2019re satisfied. Still, we keep tabs on the sect\u2019s movements, so as to feed that information to... relevant parties. </div> </div> </div>They say the Sabbat's war with other factions is functioning as a self-policing measure, but if MtA Vampires are same creatures as VtM, it is an utterly ridiculous, misguided notion. And considering the sheer depth and breadth of NWO's knowledge(they even have awarence of Tremere and nature of its Thaumaturgy - which OoH did not before the Second Massasa War) and simple fact that there are many cities controlled by Sabbat (especially in South America) and so-called &quot;Cainites&quot; rampaging with impunity and causing enormous social, political and memetic problems in those areas, it is going to be improbable if the Union do not target hemovores first and Tradition second in the Sabbat-contaminated zones.<br /> <br /> In those areas, Sabbat are the paramount threat against Consensus, direr than EDE or Werecreature incursions, and surpassing even the Marauders and Nephandi in its severity. And in South America, complete eradication of Sabbat should be the Union's top priority. And since the Sabbat's wealth and social clout is vastly insignificant compared to Camarilla, Cainites are significantly easier to exterminate than Kindred - just firebomb the vile hemovores dens, dungeons and havens with incendiaries and purge the abominations with cleansing flame.<br /> <br /> And even if the Union as whole is blind at sheer scope of Sabbat activities, its institutional contempt to the humanity, generalized disregard of Masquerade, incorrigibly chaotic nature, unequivocal monstrosity will surely cause tremendous revulsion and disgust to local Amalgams and duly warrant retributions with extreme prejudge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-05-2017, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T02:59:46-08:00","id":1155987,"title":"","content":"Well, if you're looking at the crossover information in such a way then the Sabbat are less powerful in that part of the world than they are through a purely VTM lense. South America is one of the last havens of the Fera (who really don't like vampires pissing in their pool) and also the location of some major Werewolf war zones to boot. The Sabbat have a lot more to worry about when their are packs of Bonegnawers, Glasswalkers and Uktena active in and around Mexico City not to forget the Bastet, Mokole and maybe even Naga that may well have gotten caught up in matters (especially in a place where the Masquerade is practically ignored then the Veil is a lot more flexible).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T10:16:34-08:00","id":1156085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1155936#post1155936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NWO, the designated leader of the Union, <i>know </i>there are Camarilla, Sabbat and other Sects of Vampires, feed information to relevant parties, keep tabs one them and clearly <i>spying </i>them 24/7 through whatever means(I imagine captured, Processed and Conditioned Vampire sleeper agents), and very likely possess Book of Nod. That much is explicitly stated in their CB.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They say the Sabbat's war with other factions is functioning as a self-policing measure, but if MtA Vampires are same creatures as VtM, it is an utterly ridiculous, misguided notion. And considering the sheer depth and breadth of NWO's knowledge(they even have awarence of Tremere and nature of its Thaumaturgy - which OoH did not before the Second Massasa War) and simple fact that there are many cities controlled by Sabbat (especially in South America) and so-called &quot;Cainites&quot; rampaging with impunity and causing enormous social, political and memetic problems in those areas, it is going to be improbable if the Union do not target hemovores first and Tradition second in the Sabbat-contaminated zones.<br /> <br /> In those areas, Sabbat are the paramount threat against Consensus, direr than EDE or Werecreature incursions, and surpassing even the Marauders and Nephandi in its severity. And in South America, complete eradication of Sabbat should be the Union's top priority. And since the Sabbat's wealth and social clout is vastly insignificant compared to Camarilla, Cainites are significantly easier to exterminate than Kindred - just firebomb the vile hemovores dens, dungeons and havens with incendiaries and purge the abominations with cleansing flame.<br /> <br /> And even if the Union as whole is blind at sheer scope of Sabbat activities, its institutional contempt to the humanity, generalized disregard of Masquerade, incorrigibly chaotic nature, unequivocal monstrosity will surely cause tremendous revulsion and disgust to local Amalgams and duly warrant retributions with extreme prejudge.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, you have to take into account how those books work. It doesn't mean that the NWO knows something. It means that someone at NWO knows something. Also, it isn't clear the extend of such knowledge. Just because they think they know it all, it doesn't mean they really do. This doesn't make clear in any way, as an example, that they spy on the Sabbat 24/7, that was your guess.<br /> <br /> Knowing about the Tremere also means nothing. They could either have kept better registers about old House Tremere and its end, or simply have found some by happenstance. I would lean to the later, since this guy seems to ignore the origins of the Tremere, as much as the several other variants of blood magic out there, like Koldunism.<br /> <br /> About the problems the Sabbat causes in South America, you forget that those statements are likewise made by unreliable witnesses. As much as the Sabbat causes trouble here in the setting, it isn't so obviously supernatural as you think, nor is it nearly so widespread as USA's hearsay paints it. Not to say that it isn't a fraction of the simple process you seems to think it is. The Sabbat does have wealth and social clout, just not in the same places. They are as hard to find in general as any other vampire, and they also live in cities. You can't simply firebomb their dens more than you can simply firebomb NYC.<br /> <br /> You can look for other threads on the matter of all-out-war among splats, but it isn't nearly as easy as it seems, specially when things start to escalate.<br /> <br /> In the end, it is a matter of logistics, cost and goal. A war against the Sabbat would be a Pyrrhic victory at best. It would cost too much resources, weaken the Union against their enemies, and probably hurt the Consensus far more than just letting them go. The Union seems omnipotent, but they actually have, as everyone else, their resources spread thin. Every move is a cost, and must be measured against its benefits. At all sides they have potential enemies and opportunistic parties that can and will act as flexibly as them. They are fighting a war against an organization whose sole purpose is to take down the Consensus, among with several loose groups of independent Deviants with similar goals of control of local Paradigm. Just think about how those main enemies could capitalize this kind of war. And how the other Deviants will react? A group that suddenly moves the force needed to wipe the Sabbat in such a short time would attract attention from several other parties, and they aren't likely to simply think the Technocrats are harmless pacifist while they commit supernatural genocide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T12:49:39-08:00","id":1156130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156085#post1156085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the problems the Sabbat causes in South America, you forget that those statements are likewise made by unreliable witnesses. As much as the Sabbat causes trouble here in the setting, it isn't so obviously supernatural as you think, nor is it nearly so widespread as USA's hearsay paints it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the real world, perhaps. But this is the World of Darkness, and South America is a literal hellhole, thanks to ceaseless efforts of Sabbat. And I do not live USA and English is not my native.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156085#post1156085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to say that it isn't a fraction of the simple process you seems to think it is. The Sabbat does have wealth and social clout, just not in the same places. They are as hard to find in general as any other vampire, and they also live in cities. You can't simply firebomb their dens more than you can simply firebomb NYC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firebomb NYC and firebomb obscured dens of Mexico slums is definitely not the same thing. It cannot be equated. And I have never read or heard Sabbat having wealth and social clout rivaling that of Camarilla, let alone Technocracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156085#post1156085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can look for other threads on the matter of all-out-war among splats, but it isn't nearly as easy as it seems, specially when things start to escalate.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Is there any the Union-Sabbat total war threads? </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156085#post1156085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, it is a matter of logistics, cost and goal. A war against the Sabbat would be a Pyrrhic victory at best. It would cost too much resources, weaken the Union against their enemies, and probably hurt the Consensus far more than just letting them go.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It is definitely not a Pyrrhic victory. Letting Sabbat inflict far more damage to Consensus in long term than eradicate them from face of the Earth. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156085#post1156085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Union seems omnipotent, but they actually have, as everyone else, their resources spread thin. Every move is a cost, and must be measured against its benefits. At all sides they have potential enemies and opportunistic parties that can and will act as flexibly as them.<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So do Sabbat, in fact, even more so than the Union. And Sabbat hardly possess reliable resources as an institution. It is more like a collective of packs than a veritable organization. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156085#post1156085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are fighting a war against an organization whose sole purpose is to take down the Consensus, among with several loose groups of independent Deviants with similar goals of control of local Paradigm. Just think about how those main enemies could capitalize this kind of war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since 2000, that is more like occasional skirmishes and brushfire rather than all-out conflict, and both parties are cooperating as frequently as clashing. And if the Union choose to take down Sabbat, I bet Tradition and other (sane) mage groups are going to support the Union, if not openly cooperate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156085#post1156085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And how the other Deviants will react? A group that suddenly moves the force needed to wipe the Sabbat in such a short time would attract attention from several other parties, and they aren't likely to simply think the Technocrats are harmless pacifist while they commit supernatural genocide.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It would be more appropriate supernatural pest control than genocide. No one will lament extermination of Sabbat or give succor to them. And no one will consider the Union as &quot;harmless pacifist&quot;. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Remember, it is at war with every other supernatural denizens in WoD, </span></span></span><br /> <br /> And that is the case if we assume other Deviants have a scant of credible knowledge regarding the Union. Despite its policy, there are very few, if any, other Deviants groups and factions have inkling of existence of the Union and true scope its power, reach and influence with possible exception of Marauders, Nephandi and Pentex.<br /> <br /> Even if they hear rumors about Technocracy, they will dismiss &quot;mage shadow government&quot; as false delusion, vamphiric paranoia, or worse, outright disinformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T13:58:45-08:00","id":1156153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156130#post1156130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the real world, perhaps. But this is the World of Darkness, and South America is a literal hellhole, thanks to ceaseless efforts of Sabbat. And I do not live USA and English is not my native.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about you, but about the books proper. WoD is all written from an in-setting perspective. It includes the use of a writing technique called Unreliable Narrator. Basically, the fluff is always described through the perspective of an in-setting character. As much as this character is certainly very knowledgeable, the narrative is still colored by its perspectives and intentions. That is greatly used to explain discrepancies between books both in distinct lines and, sometimes, in the same line.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, american hearsay have much to tell about descriptions from other places. Not because the reader is american, nor because the writer is american, but because the fictional narrator is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156130#post1156130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firebomb NYC and firebomb obscured dens of Mexico slums is definitely not the same thing. It cannot be equated. And I have never read or heard Sabbat having wealth and social clout rivaling that of Camarilla, let alone Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sabbat vampires don't live in obscured dens of Mexico slums. At least not only. They live spread in cities much like any other vampire. Also, the obscure dens are still located inside a city. NYC also have slums of its own, and obscure dens. By the way, it was a Sabbat stronghold for quite some time. To firebomb those places is still to be seen firebombing buildings seemingly at random. For a better example, though, you could easily substitute NYC for Detroit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156130#post1156130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Is there any the Union-Sabbat total war threads? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, but either way there are other total war threads where you can find information on hundreds of opinions from the forums about those things, including at least a dozen about Tech vs Sabbat. This isn't the firs, second, or even tenth time. Nothing against it, though, its just that you can find a lot more about this in older threads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156130#post1156130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It is definitely not a Pyrrhic victory. Letting Sabbat inflict far more damage to Consensus in long term than eradicate them from face of the Earth. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming they will one day both win over Camarilla, win over their ancients, prove they are right, survive their own victory and start to act true to what they say. It is fairly unlikely that it all will happen in the next centuries, unless Gehenna actually happens, and then the Sabbat will still be the lesser problem.<br /> <br /> Until them, the sheer amount of resources the Union would have to apply to truly obliterate the Sabbat, assuming it even possible, would render it easy prey to the Traditions, make them target for other supernaturals en masse, and probably harm the Consensus far more in the display of pure power that will ensue, since not only they will have to bring the big guns, but the Sabbat elders around the world will answer in kind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156130#post1156130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So do Sabbat, in fact, even more so than the Union. And Sabbat hardly possess reliable resources as an institution. It is more like a collective of packs than a veritable organization. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>First, I don't thing that the Sabbat would have things so thinly spread, but it isn't relevant. Any group targeted for annihilation will quickly have a huge priority on survival. Winning a local war is a simple matter. Complete extermination is far more hard to pull out. The toll it will have on the Sabbat isn't really relevant unless they survive in the end. The toll in the Union resources is the thing here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156130#post1156130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since 2000, that is more like occasional skirmishes and brushfire rather than all-out conflict, and both parties are cooperating as frequently as clashing. And if the Union choose to take down Sabbat, I bet Tradition and other (sane) mage groups are going to support the Union, if not openly cooperate.</div> </div> </div> </div>A series of circumstances brought this relative peace, but the sudden weakening of the Union would certainly change those circumstances drastically. Also, most Tradition Mages don't actually have all that interest on bringing down the Sabbat, even if they know of them. A passing interest, maybe. But not to the point of committing nearly as many resources to it. The Consensus is still their worst enemy, and an opportunity to take down the Union wouldn't be passed so lightly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156130#post1156130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be more appropriate supernatural pest control than genocide. No one will lament extermination of Sabbat or give succor to them. And no one will consider the Union as &quot;harmless pacifist&quot;. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Remember, it is at war with every other supernatural denizens in WoD, </span></span></span><br /> <br /> And that is the case if we assume other Deviants have a scant of credible knowledge regarding the Union. Despite its policy, there are very few, if any, other Deviants groups and factions have inkling of existence of the Union and true scope its power, reach and influence with possible exception of Marauders, Nephandi and Pentex.<br /> <br /> Even if they hear rumors about Technocracy, they will dismiss &quot;mage shadow government&quot; as false delusion, vamphiric paranoia, or worse, outright disinformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Short story: virtually every house in the planet get a cockroach infestation from time to time. To this, we call on pest control. In a city next to mine, something interesting happened. People first stopped calling pest control and started to apply pesticides by themselves. Then, they thought it a good idea to apply the pesticides not only in their homes, but on the sewers, so to get total extermination of cockroaches.<br /> <br /> In the next summer, attacks by Yellow Scorpions got so common that the medical services couldn't handle the sheer number of poisoned people. Luckily, it isn't a lethal poison, mind you, but it was a huge health problem nonetheless. What happened was that scorpions eat cockroaches, and without them in the sewers they started to get out in numbers.<br /> <br /> Complete annihilation of a role in the ecosystem isn't Pest Control. It causes problems. The Sabbat isn't dearly loved by many, so it isn't likely they will get much help. But they still have a niche that will be greatly disturbed. And the Union's display of destruction and disregard for them will certainly stand up. In the same vein that in NWO book the Union shows knowledge of the Sabbat, do not dismiss so quickly the other splats on having some knowledge of the Union. They do.<br /> <br /> As much as it is true that this knowledge isn't great or common, you're talking about a huge display of destruction. Other denizens of the shadows are guaranteed to notice this. Secrecy comes with subtlety, and extermination isn't subtle at all. Not even the relationship between the Fera and the Wyrm goes to such extreme, and the times it went in the past are remembered as having dread consequences. The Union will become the most obvious and instant target of the world, since no one knows any reason for them not to direct the same unbound violence upon others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T14:38:09-08:00","id":1156162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156153#post1156153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short story: virtually every house in the planet get a cockroach infestation from time to time. To this, we call on pest control. In a city next to mine, something interesting happened. People first stopped calling pest control and started to apply pesticides by themselves. Then, they thought it a good idea to apply the pesticides not only in their homes, but on the sewers, so to get total extermination of cockroaches.<br /> <br /> In the next summer, attacks by Yellow Scorpions got so common that the medical services couldn't handle the sheer number of poisoned people. Luckily, it isn't a lethal poison, mind you, but it was a huge health problem nonetheless. What happened was that scorpions eat cockroaches, and without them in the sewers they started to get out in numbers.<br /> <br /> Complete annihilation of a role in the ecosystem isn't Pest Control. It causes problems. The Sabbat isn't dearly loved by many, so it isn't likely they will get much help. But they still have a niche that will be greatly disturbed. And the Union's display of destruction and disregard for them will certainly stand up. In the same vein that in NWO book the Union shows knowledge of the Sabbat, do not dismiss so quickly the other splats on having some knowledge of the Union. They do.<br /> <br /> As much as it is true that this knowledge isn't great or common, you're talking about a huge display of destruction. Other denizens of the shadows are guaranteed to notice this. Secrecy comes with subtlety, and extermination isn't subtle at all. Not even the relationship between the Fera and the Wyrm goes to such extreme, and the times it went in the past are remembered as having dread consequences. The Union will become the most obvious and instant target of the world, since no one knows any reason for them not to direct the same unbound violence upon others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree - and I'm going to elaborate later. But which other splats show some knowledge of the Union, besides the Mage? I'm very interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-05-2017, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T15:45:26-08:00","id":1156178,"title":"","content":"Glass Walkers know there are other conspiracies on the cities. They have only passing knowledge of Mages in general, but they do guess something like the Technocracy exists.<br /> <br /> Wraiths are ghosts, they are everywhere and some of them were anything else before, including Technocrats.<br /> <br /> Changelings are extremely aware of the Technocracy, since they can sense the Banality they spread at a great distance, and it is an effect the Union isn't aware to even try to suppress.<br /> <br /> Vampire elders, including Sabbat ones, have accompanied the wars of the Magi at a distance for a long time. They do not distinguish completely between Magi and Humans, but they do know of the Order of Reason and what they are now. Specially the Tremere, they know exactly what the Union is.<br /> <br /> Back to the Fera, the Ananasi not only knows about the Union as they frequently spy on their Constructs both on Earth and on the Umbra. This Changing Breed is, maybe, the most successfully secret group in the entire WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T18:02:31-08:00","id":1156207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156178#post1156178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glass Walkers know there are other conspiracies on the cities. They have only passing knowledge of Mages in general, but they do guess something like the Technocracy exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Rev. Glass Walkers splatbook, while they know science and technology <i>are </i>magick of humanity, they do not have any knowledge of the Technocracy. Intriguingly enough, in Rev. CB, Glass Walkers proposed the Union to make an alliance, and they have knowledge about each Convention. They also know the Union are actively hunting down Werecreatures, but they still proposed alliance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156178#post1156178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraiths are ghosts, they are everywhere and some of them were anything else before, including Technocrats.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have to know about the Technocracy, both in Earth and in Umbra, and probably hate the Technocracy, since they routinely annihilate ghosts and spirits in their crosshairs. But they could do nothing against the Union, even in current weakened state, just same as they are utterly incapable of punishing Giovanni and other Necromancers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156178#post1156178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings are extremely aware of the Technocracy, since they can sense the Banality they spread at a great distance, and it is an effect the Union isn't aware to even try to suppress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of <i>course </i>they are extremely aware of the Technocracy, and very eager to undermine it. Assault against the Technocracy is among few things that can unite their feuding Courts. And the Technocracy know about Changelings, even if they do not believe in fairies. And they dearly wish to exterminate Fair Folk. And still, Fae could not do anything against the Union, and day by day they lose their Freeholds to the Union. According to C20, the Union routinely overrun and sanitize their Freeholds and trods, and they are woefully powerless to prevent it. They are not able to overthrow grasp of the Technocracy and put an end to Banality, even if the Union are distracted or in a poor shape.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156178#post1156178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire elders, including Sabbat ones, have accompanied the wars of the Magi at a distance for a long time. They do not distinguish completely between Magi and Humans, but they do know of the Order of Reason and what they are now. Specially the Tremere, they know exactly what the Union is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is news to me. Although according to the Blood Treachery, it seems that the Tremere Antediluvian has a vague notion about the Union. Anyway, could you provide reliable sources?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156178#post1156178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the Fera, the Ananasi not only knows about the Union as they frequently spy on their Constructs both on Earth and on the Umbra. This Changing Breed is, maybe, the most successfully secret group in the entire WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seriously doubt it. According to W20, Sabbat are acutely aware of existence of Ananasi, and they are planning to eliminate competitors.<br /> <br /> And if the Sabbat are aware of Ananasi, odds are every other faction having at least a passing knowledge of them, especially the Union - Strike Force Zero <i>know </i>Ananasi and Kumo, so the Union have to know Werespiders, and deal with them accordingly.<br /> <br /> And in any case, they are pose no threat whatsoever to the Union.<br /> <br /> So no, even if the Union maneuver to eradicate Sabbat, no one will, or <i>can</i>, raise a hand, especially when they make an alliance with Tradition, and threat Camarilla if they oppose eradication of Sabbat, then they are going to reveal Masquarade and inform mortal governments of existence of vampires.<br /> <br /> Wait, that is <i>exactly </i>what they have done in 5th edition. And Camarilla still could do no harm agaithe Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-06-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T21:56:07-08:00","id":1156235,"title":"","content":"In that case, you already have the answer you wanted. Clearly the Technocracy is insurmountably stronger than the rest, and completely unstoppable. They didn't won yet because they didn't wanted to.<br /> <br /> You could try to run the scenario and see how it unfolds, an RPG of sorts. Start a new thread declaring intention and a Google Docs for you to record the unfolding tale. Each time you can propose questions like this to ask people how they think things will unfold in the next step, then take your considerations and write the next step down on the doc. It would actually be an interesting process to watch and participate here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T22:16:36-08:00","id":1156239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156235#post1156235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, you already have the answer you wanted. Clearly the Technocracy is insurmountably stronger than the rest, and completely unstoppable. They didn't won yet because they didn't wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. That is the reason why I have asked this particular question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-06-2017, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:37:33-08:00","id":1156296,"title":"","content":"Well, canonically they are not unassailable and they are written as a foil (and antagonist) for the Traditions which is the core game for Mage the Ascension in which most of the other supernaturals do not take any form of center stage. Just like all the other game lines. As soon as you start going for a One World of Darkness crossover things get messier, a lot messier. The Union knows nothing about Changelings given that they literally cannot view or study fae nature and remember any of it courtesy of the Mists and a Changeling can feel a Technocrat coming a mile off. The Union already faces challenges from the Traditions and although they have the upper hand in the Ascension War they are hardly unassailable, add to this the massive challenge for resources from Vampire clans (as opposed to the occasional individual undead monster from a Mage specific angle) and the massive cross pulling in government organisations such as gets demonstrated in Project Twilight.<br /> <br /> If all that wasn't enough then they have the problem of anti-Weaver Garou and shifters getting involved not to mention minions of the Weaver itself as the educated mortals of the Union are perfect candidates for becoming Drones not to mention that a large amount of the Union's toys can run afoul of a Glasswalker pack with a minor amount of intel, nothing screws up a Mage more than a Paradox Spirit.It's worth noting that the Union has almost no counter to the Penumbra in practice, only the Void Engineers really pay much heed to DimSci and that's seemingly focused on far realms and space (but not the Aetherial Realm). The Union also has to but up against Pentex along with all the Vampiric and Tradition interference in that quarter of resources too. <br /> <br /> On top of the above for all the union has a bunch of fancy tech and toys most of it is only usable by a very few members of the Union (to whit the Mages) which, by the cannon crossover type numbers are somewhat rarer than Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T06:18:22-08:00","id":1156318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156296#post1156296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of the above for all the union has a bunch of fancy tech and toys most of it is only usable by a very few members of the Union (to whit the Mages) which, by the cannon crossover type numbers are somewhat rarer than Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Social Conditioning allows humans to use Devices, which most of their toys are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:22:50-08:00","id":1156334,"title":"","content":"Most of their toys are Foci, some of their toys are Devices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:49:43-08:00","id":1156345,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be so sure of that. The Technoracy has an awfull lot of Devices and relatively few mages-to the point that HitMarks, a special type of Device that requires several spheres at 5 to create, are treated as more expendable than the enlightened. Hence it stands to reason for most of their toys to be Devices, and some Foci (as Foci are only used by the rare breed of enlightened)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T12:57:54-08:00","id":1156447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156296#post1156296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, canonically they are not unassailable and they are written as a foil (and antagonist) for the Traditions which is the core game for Mage the Ascension in which most of the other supernaturals do not take any form of center stage. Just like all the other game lines. As soon as you start going for a One World of Darkness crossover things get messier, a lot messier. The Union knows nothing about Changelings given that they literally cannot view or study fae nature and remember any of it courtesy of the Mists and a Changeling can feel a Technocrat coming a mile off. The Union already faces challenges from the Traditions and although they have the upper hand in the Ascension War they are hardly unassailable, add to this the massive challenge for resources from Vampire clans (as opposed to the occasional individual undead monster from a Mage specific angle) and the massive cross pulling in government organisations such as gets demonstrated in Project Twilight.<br /> <br /> If all that wasn't enough then they have the problem of anti-Weaver Garou and shifters getting involved not to mention minions of the Weaver itself as the educated mortals of the Union are perfect candidates for becoming Drones not to mention that a large amount of the Union's toys can run afoul of a Glasswalker pack with a minor amount of intel, nothing screws up a Mage more than a Paradox Spirit.It's worth noting that the Union has almost no counter to the Penumbra in practice, only the Void Engineers really pay much heed to DimSci and that's seemingly focused on far realms and space (but not the Aetherial Realm). The Union also has to but up against Pentex along with all the Vampiric and Tradition interference in that quarter of resources too.<br /> <br /> On top of the above for all the union has a bunch of fancy tech and toys most of it is only usable by a very few members of the Union (to whit the Mages) which, by the cannon crossover type numbers are somewhat rarer than Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Canonically</i>, Mage is far more common than Garou. Ratio of True Mage per normal human is 1:150,000, while Garou per human is 1:500,000. And if we take conservative estimation provided from Malcom Shepherd, there exist 1 Mage per 200,000 unAwakened. The truth is, Mage are among <i>common </i>supernaturals, and their numbers are many. And that is one of reasons why the Ascension War has not ended yet - each party has enough cannon fodders to continue respective group's operations indefinitely.<br /> <br /> And the Union have always got the lion's share along with the Tradition.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the Union employ awful lot of Extraordinary Citizen and Sympathizers, which are hedge Technomancers and Conditioned humans respectively. Among the Union, proportion of the Enlightened members could be measured in a single digit, while the rest are Extraordinary and Sympathizers who utilize mass-produced Devises manufactured and supplied by the Union.<br /> <br /> Hell, the Unionists most of their enemies would likely be encountered and fought are Extraordinary, Sympathizers and constructs, <i>not </i>Enlightened Citizen. For instance, In fact, vast majority of its activities, including military operations, are conducted by un-Awakened members, both in the Earthside and in Umbra.<br /> <br /> In this aspect, the Traditions and other Mage factions are akin to the Union, even though they are usually more elitist and degree of Sleeper integration is lesser. Support personnel such as <i>consor</i>, <i>grog </i>and <i>familiar </i>are vastly outnumbering True Mage in any Mage group, and they are more useful than, as it were, kinfolks by far.<br /> <br /> And no, canonically the Union's toys are composed of Devise, Gadget and Invention. Only usage of Invention and <i>extremely </i>complex Devises, such as Void Engineers Universal vessels, are restricted to Awakened members. And Gadgets could often be used by normal Sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-06-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T14:28:35-08:00","id":1156477,"title":"","content":"Okay, I mixed my Vampire-Garou-Mage number estimates and I'll cede the ground on Devices (in fact i feel stupid for having written it guven HitMarks, MiB, the Book of the Weaver etc) but everything else stands. The reason the Union hasn't stomped down on everyone is either A) In full crossover they simpley can't because in full crossover the world is far more complex and the Unions power is less monolithic (and its only monolithic when playing Traditions game, on the other side you see the cracks and divides) in the face of so much more to actively have to deal with (again losing people to the OneSong is going to be a perpetual problem) and the Consensus being far less a prevailing factor or B) You're playing Mage and the supernatural creatures have already been effectively purged to the point where they're more of an occasional thing and the Ascension War us the focus of the thing. Anything else is your own interpretation of things for your own table, but you're not going to find a canon crossover reason for them not doing it other than they cannot and to attempt to do so would use far too much in the way of resources, manpower and other assets to be feasible, at least while also fighting the Ascension War, dealing with the Traditions, Marauders and Nephandi, furthering self Enlightment through advancing SCIENCE! And trying to keep to the TimeTable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T15:18:18-08:00","id":1156497,"title":"","content":"Hit-Marks are actually something between a Device and a really fucked-up mind-wiped Enlightened, usually artificial, anyways. But yeah, most of the rest stands.<br /> <br /> The numbers aren't clear. The single splat with actual hard numbers put on are Vampires, with 1:100,000 on the core. And even then, the actual fluctuation of such number is completely unknown. Several people did guesses about the actual numbers of the night-folks, some really well-informed. But they stand as guesses. Vampires seem to be the most common splat, with the possibility of Demon overthrowing them as they reach Earth, since their number in Hell is unknown (and guessed even higher than Mortals by some) and they are really hard to kill for good (or even to know that you have to kill them for good).<br /> <br /> In the Guide to Technocracy <i>the last standing book with official stand until 5e is released</i>, it is said that the Union is far weaker than it seems, with the image of supreme strength being one of its most powerful weapons in the Ascension War. In theory, the Traditions have the upper hand in resources, but almost complete inability to use it collectively if compared to the Union. Also, the Union do have the advantage on Devices and such, since they developed systems to put them in <u>seemingly</u> mass production. As a rule of thumb, their unEnlightened members are far more armed than the Tradition's unAwakened in general.<br /> <br /> What the book opens from there is a lot of options to add complexity to logistics. The upper hand comes actually from a far superior scheme to manage and employ resources, among with, well, unity. Without going to details, it stands up to question if the toys of the Traditions average to more actual power or not.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Vampires, Changelings, Werewolves and Demons, just to say about the ones I know better, are not only <b>also</b> able to amass mortal servants, but actually have them <b>stronger</b> than what Magi do. A single drop of a Vampire's blood makes at least any mamal into a ghoul for an entire month. It means Potence 1 instantly at no further cost whatsoever, and the possibility to teach other Disciplines, beyond access to any feat of the Blood. A Magi needs far more work just to work shit in front of the mortal's eyes, even a Technocrat. As much as they are sacred to the Changing Breeds, fetishes are far easier for them to produce, they even have some Kinfolk that can do the job, and Kinfolk are naturally numerous. I concede that they have it harder to get more mystical power than that for themselves, but on the other hand they, the Kinfolk, have one of the greatest hinted networks in the WoD, meaning an ability to coordinate that makes the Union pale in comparison. Changelings can enhance mortals even easier than Vampires, and discard easier yet if they need to, so they won't even remember shit to tell. Actually, the fae have the easier time to turn a Magi into a servant without attracting attention. Demonic Thralls are a little harder to create, but not harder than unEnlightened Technomancers, and their power level is simply ludicrous for &quot;human servant splats&quot;.<br /> <br /> But nothing here matters. I already proposed a compromise that would be fun for all of us. Create the starting situation, the move on the Union's part, and lets discuss it step by step. I'm already seeing where it will end, but the trip will be funnier than repeating all those arguments again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T18:38:43-08:00","id":1156532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156497#post1156497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hit-Marks are actually something between a Device and a really fucked-up mind-wiped Enlightened, usually artificial, anyways. But yeah, most of the rest stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Atlas Hit-Marks are &quot;really fucked-up mind-wiped Enlightened.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156497#post1156497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The numbers aren't clear. The single splat with actual hard numbers put on are Vampires, with 1:100,000 on the core. And even then, the actual fluctuation of such number is completely unknown. Several people did guesses about the actual numbers of the night-folks, some really well-informed. But they stand as guesses. Vampires seem to be the most common splat, with the possibility of Demon overthrowing them as they reach Earth, since their number in Hell is unknown (and guessed even higher than Mortals by some) and they are really hard to kill for good (or even to know that you have to kill them for good).</div> </div> </div> </div>Another splats with actual hard numbers put on are Mage and Werewolf, 150,000 to one and 500,000 to one respectively. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156497#post1156497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Guide to Technocracy <i>the last standing book with official stand until 5e is released</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot comprehend what do you intend to mean. So M20 and Rev. are non-canon? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156497#post1156497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it is said that the Union is far weaker than it seems, with the image of supreme strength being one of its most powerful weapons in the Ascension War. In theory, the Traditions have the upper hand in resources, but almost complete inability to use it collectively if compared to the Union. Also, the Union do have the advantage on Devices and such, since they developed systems to put them in <u>seemingly</u> mass production. As a rule of thumb, their unEnlightened members are far more armed than the Tradition's unAwakened in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>GttT was released during 2nd Edition. By then, ratio of Mage per mortal was 1 to 1,000,000, instead of Rev. 1 to 150,000 or Malcom's 1 to 200,000. Back then both the Union and Traditions were comprised of a few thousands of Mage. <br /> <br /> While I agree the image of omnipotence is one of the greatest weapon of the Union in the Ascension War, I have never seen or heard anything indicating or alluding that the Traditions possess more resources than the Union. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156497#post1156497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the book opens from there is a lot of options to add complexity to logistics. The upper hand comes actually from a far superior scheme to manage and employ resources, among with, well, unity. Without going to details, it stands up to question if the toys of the Traditions average to more actual power or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>You caught it accurately. The Union is the most organized, coherent, united and supremely managed faction on the Earth, and that is one of their primary advantage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156497#post1156497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, Vampires, Changelings, Werewolves and Demons, just to say about the ones I know better, are not only <b>also</b> able to amass mortal servants, but actually have them <b>stronger</b> than what Magi do. A single drop of a Vampire's blood makes at least any mamal into a ghoul for an entire month. It means Potence 1 instantly at no further cost whatsoever, and the possibility to teach other Disciplines, beyond access to any feat of the Blood. A Magi needs far more work just to work shit in front of the mortal's eyes, even a Technocrat. As much as they are sacred to the Changing Breeds, fetishes are far easier for them to produce. They even have some Kinfolk that can do the job, and Kinfolk are naturally numerous. I concede that they have it harder to get more mystical power than that for themselves, but on the other hand they, the Kinfolk, have one of the greatest hinted networks in the WoD, meaning an ability to coordinate that makes the Union pale in comparison. Changelings can enhance mortals even easier than Vampires, and discard easier yet if they need to, so they won't even remember shit to tell. Actually, the fae have the easier time to turn a Magi into a servant without attracting attention. Demonic Thralls are a little harder to create, but not harder than unEnlightened Technomancers, and their power level is simply ludicrous for &quot;human servant splats&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is irrelevant. Among them, only vampires and mage are utilizing their mortal servants effectively and with large number. Vaunted network of Kinfolk is paled when compared to the network of Ghouls and Sympathizers, both are far more integrated into mortal society and in literally everywhere. And Kinfolk are unable to counter such deeply entrenched influence. And most of the Union's socio-political power is derived from legions of well-placed Sympathizers, augmented with Extraordinary. In every Extraordinary, there are scores of Sympathizers. And I'm sure there will be a lot more Sympathizes than Kinfolk and Ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T19:31:12-08:00","id":1156545,"title":"","content":"Do you get any sources for what you say?<br /> <br /> Anyhow, did ye get the answers to your OP?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T01:16:27-08:00","id":1156610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156178#post1156178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the Fera, the Ananasi not only knows about the Union as they frequently spy on their Constructs both on Earth and on the Umbra. This Changing Breed is, maybe, the most successfully secret group in the entire WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what you think that the Ananasi are the most successfull group in the World of Darkness in regards to maintaining secrecy? Is it something written in the Ananasi Breed Book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T01:18:46-08:00","id":1156611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156545#post1156545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you get any sources for what you say?</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly do you say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T03:36:07-08:00","id":1156625,"title":"","content":"By the way Guide to the Technocracy also flat out states that it doesn't have the resources to maintain dealing with the Traditions at the level it is and declare war in the undead. They're also ignorant of the threats of the Weaver and Wyrm and has lost more than one Amalgam through spiritual corruption alone not to mention the problems with Syndicate involvement in Pentex. Changelings don't exist for the union and any agent saying otherwise needs to check in for re-education afterall even f there are some fairies about they couldnt possinly posevs threat, some of the Kithain societies on the other hand may have learned a thing or two about the Union and don't like what they have seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T05:20:49-08:00","id":1156639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156610#post1156610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on what you think that the Ananasi are the most successfull group in the World of Darkness in regards to maintaining secrecy? Is it something written in the Ananasi Breed Book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Several sources cite the Ananasi on passing, but have too little information even in comparison on what they have on others. The greater mystery is their numbers, that can range from anything between a few dozens in the world to actually the greatest sentient population on Earth. Their Breed Book cite their dealings with vampires, mingling in the undead society completely, to the point of taking part on Elysium, while Union Constructs are completely open to them, since they treat the Gauntlet in a reversed manner.<br /> <br /> But I didn't meant that this was overtly stated anywhere, hence the &quot;maybe&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156611#post1156611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly do you say?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you point books and pages for your info?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T09:18:02-08:00","id":1156710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156639#post1156639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) while Union Constructs are completely open to them, since they treat the Gauntlet in a reversed manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that just treating the Gauntlet in a reversed manner would be enough for the Ananasi to be able to go into the Technocracy's Constructs whenever they want and unopposed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:05:14-08:00","id":1156734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156625#post1156625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way Guide to the Technocracy also flat out states that it doesn't have the resources to maintain dealing with the Traditions at the level it is and declare war in the undead. They're also ignorant of the threats of the Weaver and Wyrm and has lost more than one Amalgam through spiritual corruption alone not to mention the problems with Syndicate involvement in Pentex. Changelings don't exist for the union and any agent saying otherwise needs to check in for re-education afterall even f there are some fairies about they couldnt possinly posevs threat, some of the Kithain societies on the other hand may have learned a thing or two about the Union and don't like what they have seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is all before Avatar Storm/Revised, let alone M20. And like I said, back then Mage population were far fewer than Rev. and M20, thanks to ratio. And no, read C20 and Rev. CB. Union know Fae, even if they do not believe in fairies, and deal with them case-by-case. Some in the Union wish to completely exterminate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-07-2017, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:06:58-08:00","id":1156736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156639#post1156639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you point books and pages for your info?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, for what info exactly? Mage to mortal ratio? See Mage: Les Vegas and Malcolm Shepherd's article respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:39:39-08:00","id":1156745,"title":"","content":"Posthumanity, you have already made up your mind on the matter and are choosing to willfully ignore any of the written or presented evidence on why the Union hasn't simply wiped out every trace of every supernatural creature what so ever on the planet, turned them all into Union tools, won every war on the planet, directly control every government on the planet and so forth. Stating that the GttT is pre Avatar Storm and M20 is irrelevant as there's been nothing contradict it's base facts and as such is still (currently) the main Technocracy reference book. This is also ignoring the fact that the Avatar Storm and mechanics in Revised made life massively more difficult for the Technocracy as Paradox becomes more of a problem for the Technocratic Union and some of their BIG resources were Umbral based accessible only by a few in the first place (given how rare DimSci is) and made even harder to access with the effects of the Avatar Storm. Not forgetting that the powers in control of the Union were cut off from Earth just like the masters of the Traditions. <br /> <br /> The entire purpose of this thread is meaningless as you don't want an answer to your initial 4 questions as you don't want to know Why to any of these things. What you want is an endorsement from the community of your own personal choice that that none of these things are have been done merely because the Union doesn't want to out of pique alone despite being 100% absolutely capable of doing all of these things and you want people to tell you that the written material also completely supports this. Well, that simply is not going to happen. At your table, with your own group the Gold and Silver rules apply, and that's fine, but beyond that? It's simply not supported.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T12:00:04-08:00","id":1156754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156745#post1156745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Posthumanity, you have already made up your mind on the matter and are choosing to willfully ignore any of the written or presented evidence on why the Union hasn't simply wiped out every trace of every supernatural creature what so ever on the planet, turned them all into Union tools, won every war on the planet, directly control every government on the planet and so forth. Stating that the GttT is pre Avatar Storm and M20 is irrelevant as there's been nothing contradict it's base facts and as such is still (currently) the main Technocracy reference book. This is also ignoring the fact that the Avatar Storm and mechanics in Revised made life massively more difficult for the Technocracy as Paradox becomes more of a problem for the Technocratic Union and some of their BIG resources were Umbral based accessible only by a few in the first place (given how rare DimSci is) and made even harder to access with the effects of the Avatar Storm. Not forgetting that the powers in control of the Union were cut off from Earth just like the masters of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The entire purpose of this thread is meaningless as you don't want an answer to your initial 4 questions as you don't want to know Why to any of these things. What you want is an endorsement from the community of your own personal choice that that none of these things are have been done merely because the Union doesn't want to out of pique alone despite being 100% absolutely capable of doing all of these things and you want people to tell you that the written material also completely supports this. Well, that simply is not going to happen. At your table, with your own group the Gold and Silver rules apply, and that's fine, but beyond that? It's simply not supported.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I do not willfully ignore evidence. And I have <i>already</i> gotten the answer of three out four questions. What I have asked is why the Union do not wage a total war against vampires, especially Sabbat, and eradicate them despite obvious threat it presents to Consensus. I simply wonder why the Union could not ended supernatural menace even their own line.<br /> <br /> But yes, I can see where this discussion is going...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-08-2017, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T16:12:24-08:00","id":1156828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156754#post1156754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I do not willfully ignore evidence. And I have <i>already</i> gotten the answer of three questions. What I have asked is why the Union do not wage a total war against vampires, especially Sabbat, and eradicate them despite obvious threat it presents to Consensus. I simply wonder why the Union could not ended supernatural threat even their own line.<br /> <br /> But yes, I can see where this discussion is going...</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that we got to it.<br /> <br /> Your interpretation of the lore is as valid as anything else. But you're arguing for quite a time now with the fact that others simply disagree with them. You repeatedly states your interpretation and just say that ours are outright wrong.<br /> <br /> We can solve that in two ways. The first I already proposed, and that was serious. Lets put our thoughts on proof. That would be interesting, would be fun to take part in, and give the nearest to an experimental evidence to the question. Nothing really solid, but at least would be a fun thing to do.<br /> <br /> The second is to present sources at every statement. I didn't it before, I know, I didn't thought it would be necessary. But if it is, I'll start to do.<br /> <br /> If neither works for you, then it's it. We already told you our answers. If they don't serve your vision, you'll have to find your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T02:07:56-08:00","id":1156931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156828#post1156828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that we got to it.<br /> <br /> Your interpretation of the lore is as valid as anything else. But you're arguing for quite a time now with the fact that others simply disagree with them. You repeatedly states your interpretation and just say that ours are outright wrong.<br /> <br /> We can solve that in two ways. The first I already proposed, and that was serious. Lets put our thoughts on proof. That would be interesting, would be fun to take part in, and give the nearest to an experimental evidence to the question. Nothing really solid, but at least would be a fun thing to do.<br /> <br /> The second is to present sources at every statement. I didn't it before, I know, I didn't thought it would be necessary. But if it is, I'll start to do.<br /> <br /> If neither works for you, then it's it. We already told you our answers. If they don't serve your vision, you'll have to find your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not &quot;ours&quot; or &quot;others&quot;, but &quot;yours&quot; would be correct.<br /> <br /> And haven't I already presented proofs for each statement? It is your turn to present basis of your claims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T15:35:49-08:00","id":1157140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156710#post1156710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that just treating the Gauntlet in a reversed manner would be enough for the Ananasi to be able to go into the Technocracy's Constructs whenever they want and unopposed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, but I personally think it a reasonable guess that they do sometimes. Most of the Union don't go too much into DS, and the main defense of Earth Constructs is a high Gauntlet. But the main reason I think the Ananasi could pull this off, and [u]maybe[/b] be the most successful in secrecy, is that their specialty is to go completely inconspicuous about their things. Their numbers is unknown precisely because of it.<br /> <br /> But, of course, this is completely open to interpretation. The only canon on this is that little is known of their numbers and actions, and that they are very individualistic on their endeavors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1156931#post1156931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not &quot;ours&quot; or &quot;others&quot;, but &quot;yours&quot; would be correct.<br /> <br /> And haven't I already presented proofs for each statement? It is your turn to present basis of your claims.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't argued against you since my first post on page 2, only commented on other's peoples posts. There are some other people since page 1 arguing that the Union can't do this. You say it can. You didn't proved anything, neither did I. I figured you wouldn't listen long ago, but tried to help without offending. Since I'm not sure about when it is reasonable to quit, I'm posting once more, but that's it. As crazy as I am, I'm done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T17:03:32-08:00","id":1157154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157140#post1157140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair, but I personally think it a reasonable guess that they do sometimes. Most of the Union don't go too much into DS, and the main defense of Earth Constructs is a high Gauntlet. But the main reason I think the Ananasi could pull this off, and [u]maybe[/b] be the most successful in secrecy, is that their specialty is to go completely inconspicuous about their things. Their numbers is unknown precisely because of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How well can they spy on Technocrats depends very little on their relationship with the Gauntlet and more on how well a given Construct wants to protect itself.<br /> <br /> For instance, their relation to the Gauntlet won't help against an artificialy raised one. Dimensional Science ALSO treats the Gauntlet in reverse (with science places as easy, and forests as very difficult), but an artificialy raised Gauntelt would blind them too (the only difference it's the relation between the increase and the base diff, it's the base what's reversed). Also that DimSci 1-2 is nowhere near as rare as levels 3+, to the point that one classic MiB rote uses DimSci 1.<br /> <br /> Now, I think that infiltrating in a street level Construct wouldn't be terribly hard for an Ananasi. The security is set against mages, perhaps against spirits (that are often summoned by mages), not against Fera. Prime detection it's a problem on the material side of the Gauntlet (technocratic sensors will sense the Gnosis) but the other side may have fewer defenses (increased Gauntlet does make sense).<br /> Then again, those places aren't where the real shit gets debated, if important Technocrats really want to defend against spying, Spheres provide plenty of options. And they seem to want that, think that the rank and file refers to their superiors as a myth (&quot;the hidden masters&quot;, Control)-the average agent may have more proof of the existence of vampires than the existence of their own leadership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-08-2017, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T18:20:05-08:00","id":1157162,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the problem with the Sabbat has nothing to do with the chances that Technocrats have in a vs match.<br /> <br /> The problem it's that it doesn't jive well with a society of supposedly &quot;well intended but flawed&quot; people to prioritize the Traditions more than the Sabbat. This problem comes as a consequence of several facts:<br /> 1. The traditions were &quot;defeated&quot; in revised (they tried to avoid angering the technocracy)<br /> 2. The things that the Sabbat does, and the way they do it, it's right on the ballpark of the original purpose of the Technocracy. They're cults of monsters that prey on humans, they're no better than Mistridge or a dragon.<br /> 3. The most cursory investigation on supernatural activity on Sabbat areas would lead to discover what these vampires do, and that it doesn't stop. This can be discovered by accident while investigating shady cults and suspicious murders. Even if you can't know this is part of a larguer conspiracy, as an issolated fact it's monstrous enough to require more atention than the hermetic selling self help books.<br /> 4. The Technocrats supposedly care about humans in a less than abstract fashion. They're not &quot;souless&quot; anymore (at least not on average)<br /> <br /> Let's think about it with an example: Lets say a capable street agent (like a PC could easily be) it's investigating a shady cult that opperates within a cartel. It could easily be a Traditionalist waging for power in the criminal organization, but the lead takes the agent to a blood cult of Serpents of the Light related to the Sabbat...The Agent can't know right of the bat that these aren't Traditionalists or related to the Traditons (and even if he knew, why would that prevent further investigation?...oh, it's not Mage, best leave the setting). Further investigation leads the agent to discover that they are vampires...and the things they do to humans. He manages to flee with the info without being flayed alive...barely.<br /> <br /> And he goes back to the Construct and says<b> &quot;I've observed that the vampires never cause Paradox and always kill all human witnesses and thus the Consensus it's protected. Everything it's under control&quot;</b>.<br /> <br /> ...See the problem.<br /> <br /> Those words, no matter how flawed the Agent is, are the words of the kind of &quot;souless agent of conformity&quot; that the Traditions say Technocrats are.<br /> If technocrats are supposed to care about humans, they can't have such a reaction with vampires. More so, it doesn't matter if the Technocrats can win or not, they should at least give their best try to stop it-prioritizing the defeated hippies over that sounds cheap <hr /><br /> The original Guide of the Technocracy had one possible scapegoat:<br /> <br /> The rift between the street agents that see how things are and the hidden masters that see the big picture. The agents may think vampires are very dangerous, but the leaders won't because they aren't interfering with the <u>long term goals</u> (which comprises a global chess game between the Masters of the Traditions and the Union that the Union it's currently winning). The masters are detached from things like &quot;baths of blood&quot; and the &quot;gore&quot; that agents regularly face. A few thouzands of lives don't matter to the ones that oversee millons.<br /> <br /> In the previous example, the Agent wouldn't be unfazled. He would grab his pen and writte a hundred of very serious memos to the Union asking for the eradication of the sect with extreme prejudice...and would find his petition to be rejected because it doesn't further the long therm goals of the local Symposium (that may be along the lines of expanding the drug business so the resources can go to build more starships for a conflict in Pluto or something like that-And you're planning to attack it, yeah, no, sorry, can't allow you to do that)<br /> Then the Construct may decide to take action (to the extent that they can do this without endangering the cartel itself), but they would be more or less on their own-without the impossible display of pure power that the Union sometimes show backing them. That's where the PC enter and save the day.<br /> <br /> There are other scapegoats:<br /> *Technephandi (or simply evil technocrats) that work with the Sabbat impeding the Union from taking action, deleting archives, and generally making noise.<br /> *In M20, the Traditions being very much undefeated and still a treath whereas the Civil War is still brewing. All of which keeps resources from do-gooder's hands","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-08-2017, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T19:00:14-08:00","id":1157171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157140#post1157140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't argued against you since my first post on page 2, only commented on other's peoples posts. There are some other people since page 1 arguing that the Union can't do this. You say it can. You didn't proved anything, neither did I. I figured you wouldn't listen long ago, but tried to help without offending. Since I'm not sure about when it is reasonable to quit, I'm posting once more, but that's it. As crazy as I am, I'm done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, a single person. And I have always provided ample evidences to backup my position, whereas you and he have persistently failed to do so, and intransigently ignoring my contradictions and arguments.<br /> <br /> I'm done with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-09-2017, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T19:06:05-08:00","id":1157174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157162#post1157162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, the problem with the Sabbat has nothing to do with the chances that Technocrats have in a vs match.<br /> <br /> The problem it's that it doesn't jive well with a society of supposedly &quot;well intended but flawed&quot; people to prioritize the Traditions more than the Sabbat. This problem comes as a consequence of several facts:<br /> 1. The traditions were &quot;defeated&quot; in revised (they tried to avoid angering the technocracy)<br /> 2. The things that the Sabbat does, and the way they do it, it's right on the ballpark of the original purpose of the Technocracy. They're cults of monsters that prey on humans, they're no better than Mistridge or a dragon.<br /> 3. The most cursory investigation on supernatural activity on Sabbat areas would lead to discover what these vampires do, and that it doesn't stop. This can be discovered by accident while investigating shady cults and suspicious murders. Even if you can't know this is part of a larguer conspiracy, as an issolated fact it's monstrous enough to require more atention than the hermetic selling self help books.<br /> 4. The Technocrats supposedly care about humans in a less than abstract fashion. They're not &quot;souless&quot; anymore (at least not on average)<br /> <br /> Let's think about it with an example: Lets say a capable street agent (like a PC could easily be) it's investigating a shady cult that opperates within a cartel. It could easily be a Traditionalist waging for power in the criminal organization, but the lead takes the agent to a blood cult of Serpents of the Light related to the Sabbat...The Agent can't know right of the bat that these aren't Traditionalists or related to the Traditons (and even if he knew, why would that prevent further investigation?...oh, it's not Mage, best leave the setting). Further investigation leads the agent to discover that they are vampires...and the things they do to humans. He manages to flee with the info without being flayed alive...barely.<br /> <br /> And he goes back to the Construct and says<b> &quot;I've observed that the vampires never cause Paradox and always kill all human witnesses and thus the Consensus it's protected. Everything it's under control&quot;</b>.<br /> <br /> ...See the problem.<br /> <br /> Those words, no matter how flawed the Agent is, are the words of the kind of &quot;souless agent of conformity&quot; that the Traditions say Technocrats are.<br /> If technocrats are supposed to care about humans, they can't have such a reaction with vampires. More so, it doesn't matter if the Technocrats can win or not, they should at least give their best try to stop it-prioritizing the defeated hippies over that sounds cheap <hr /><br /> The original Guide of the Technocracy had one possible scapegoat:<br /> <br /> The rift between the street agents that see how things are and the hidden masters that see the big picture. The agents may think vampires are very dangerous, but the leaders won't because they aren't interfering with the <u>long term goals</u> (which comprises a global chess game between the Masters of the Traditions and the Union that the Union it's currently winning). The masters are detached from things like &quot;baths of blood&quot; and the &quot;gore&quot; that agents regularly face. A few thouzands of lives don't matter to the ones that oversee millons.<br /> <br /> In the previous example, the Agent wouldn't be unfazled. He would grab his pen and writte a hundred of very serious memos to the Union asking for the eradication of the sect with extreme prejudice...and would find his petition to be rejected because it doesn't further the long therm goals of the local Symposium (that may be along the lines of expanding the drug business so the resources can go to build more starships for a conflict in Pluto or something like that-And you're planning to attack it, yeah, no, sorry, can't allow you to do that)<br /> Then the Construct may decide to take action (to the extent that they can do this without endangering the cartel itself), but they would be more or less on their own-without the impossible display of pure power that the Union sometimes show backing them. That's where the PC enter and save the day.<br /> <br /> There are other scapegoats:<br /> *Technephandi (or simply evil technocrats) that work with the Sabbat impeding the Union from taking action, deleting archives, and generally making noise.<br /> *In M20, the Traditions being very much undefeated and still a treath whereas the Civil War is still brewing. All of which keeps resources from do-gooder's hands</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. That is the pith of my question. If normal Technocrats are not soulless, why on earth the Union are letting Sabbat to commit their heinous reality crime with impunity? In M20, while the Traditions are still undefeated, the Union is on the substantially stronger position than Revised, and in Rev. CB, the Union still have not moved to stomp out vile atrocities of Sabbat, let alone eradicate the very root of evil.<br /> <br /> And since the Revised is not correlated with V20 in any way, so-called &quot;crossover sensibilities&quot; is no excuse.<br /> <br /> I'm fully expecting to Technocracy Reloaded will present revised, much-changed overview and attitude against vampires, and M20 and 5th edition have already alluded the Union's newfound stance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-09-2017, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T22:01:34-08:00","id":1157193,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat existing in the Technocrancy World is problematic, so it's easier to assume that crossovers don't always fit well, and that they are far less common then in VtM canon. <br /> <br /> But if you really need game-line compatibility, you can always have it be that the leaders of the technocracy, &quot;Control,&quot; have an interest in keeping the Sabbat around. Maybe as a way to keep a handle on the Camarilla. Like, first we finish off the dying traditions, then we'll deal with infinitely spawning, paradox ignoring monstrosities, and it'll be much easier to deal with Sabbat vampires who don't hide, and lack resources than with Cam vamps who are really sneaky and have tons of resources.<br /> <br /> This way you have the plucky young agent railing against the system &quot;But theyre killing people! Theyre MONSTERS!&quot; and the callous Technocratic leaders who are playing the long game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11894-shushu","name":"Shushu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T02:27:21-08:00","id":1157224,"title":"","content":"It IS possible. The Technocratic leaders think in very much &quot;elder timespan&quot;. They have whole task forces seeing the future 24/7 to triple check any course of action.They see this WoD in precarious balance and think how they can subtly manipulate it to their advantage. It's not foolish (albeit not entirely wise either) to think that they do know something we don't know. Perhaps they were doing stuff in the shadows, perhaps Ventrue paranoia about &quot;hidden masters&quot; that aren't kindred but want to control vampiric affairs isn't unfounded...<br /> <br /> In revised there were factions within the Union that wanted to be more active on the vampie hunting side. This went paralel to the weakning of Control's grasp due to the Avatar Storm. This isn't a coincidence, these fractions are composed of plucky young agents that normaly would be doomed to the low ranks but, due to the Storm killing a lot of high ups, ended taking places of relative importance when the Technocracy had to reset the whole chain of command. Still in revised you have the whole reorganization thing where the Technos were pulling their act together after the Storm.<br /> <br /> That being said it is entirely possible for the Technocracy to change their focus, eventually. Hey, they're behind the &quot;new Inquisition&quot; of 5th edition, so that's something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-09-2017, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T04:01:48-08:00","id":1157240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157224#post1157224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It IS possible. The Technocratic leaders think in very much &quot;elder timespan&quot;. They have whole task forces seeing the future 24/7 to triple check any course of action.They see this WoD in precarious balance and think how they can subtly manipulate it to their advantage. It's not foolish (albeit not entirely wise either) to think that they do know something we don't know. Perhaps they were doing stuff in the shadows, perhaps Ventrue paranoia about &quot;hidden masters&quot; that aren't kindred but want to control vampiric affairs isn't unfounded...<br /> <br /> In revised there were factions within the Union that wanted to be more active on the vampie hunting side. This went paralel to the weakning of Control's grasp due to the Avatar Storm. This isn't a coincidence, these fractions are composed of plucky young agents that normaly would be doomed to the low ranks but, due to the Storm killing a lot of high ups, ended taking places of relative importance when the Technocracy had to reset the whole chain of command. Still in revised you have the whole reorganization thing where the Technos were pulling their act together after the Storm.<br /> <br /> That being said it is entirely possible for the Technocracy to change their focus, eventually. Hey, they're behind the &quot;new Inquisition&quot; of 5th edition, so that's something.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Iteration X and Progenitors have shifted their policy to hemovores, NWO and Syndicate are still cleaving to original &quot;observe, do not engage&quot; policy regarding bloodsuckers.<br /> <br /> And Void Engineers are too busy to fight off Threat Null and repulse EDE incursions to eradicate bloodsuckers.<br /> <br /> However, M20 unequivocally states the Union is actively waging war upon vampires, werebeasts, and other diverse Night-folk.<br /> <br /> And 5th edition...well, the Union is behind the entire &quot;Second Inquisition&quot; affairs. In fact, it seems that in 5th edition, the main priority of the Union is the vampires, instead of mage. And I would certainly not be surprised if majority of the institution's personnel, gears, equipment, military hardware, operational budget and various other resources are directly supplied, fitted and organized by the Union. I'm anticipating relationship between the Union and the Second Inquisition would be similar to the SCP Foundation and its Mobile Task Forces.<br /> <br /> BTW, I have always wondered why VE's NSC have not swarmed Venice and exterminated Giovanni from the root to branch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-09-2017, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T09:05:28-08:00","id":1157293,"title":"","content":"Dude, if you want to run your game where the Technocrats exterminate every last Vampire on earth, just do it already. Get it out of your system. You've been on this particular tear for so long now that it's getting genuinely tiresome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T14:13:28-08:00","id":1157354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157293#post1157293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, if you want to run your game where the Technocrats exterminate every last Vampire on earth, just do it already. Get it out of your system. You've been on this particular tear for so long now that it's getting genuinely tiresome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have already done it in my campaign, so don't worry; vampires are not gone completely extinct yet, but they are mostly eradicated and an nuisance at the worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T14:48:27-08:00","id":1157366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157154#post1157154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How well can they spy on Technocrats depends very little on their relationship with the Gauntlet and more on how well a given Construct wants to protect itself.<br /> <br /> For instance, their relation to the Gauntlet won't help against an artificialy raised one. Dimensional Science ALSO treats the Gauntlet in reverse (with science places as easy, and forests as very difficult), but an artificialy raised Gauntelt would blind them too (the only difference it's the relation between the increase and the base diff, it's the base what's reversed). Also that DimSci 1-2 is nowhere near as rare as levels 3+, to the point that one classic MiB rote uses DimSci 1.<br /> <br /> Now, I think that infiltrating in a street level Construct wouldn't be terribly hard for an Ananasi. The security is set against mages, perhaps against spirits (that are often summoned by mages), not against Fera. Prime detection it's a problem on the material side of the Gauntlet (technocratic sensors will sense the Gnosis) but the other side may have fewer defenses (increased Gauntlet does make sense).<br /> Then again, those places aren't where the real shit gets debated, if important Technocrats really want to defend against spying, Spheres provide plenty of options. And they seem to want that, think that the rank and file refers to their superiors as a myth (&quot;the hidden masters&quot;, Control)-the average agent may have more proof of the existence of vampires than the existence of their own leadership.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairly pointed.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157162#post1157162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, the problem with the Sabbat has nothing to do with the chances that Technocrats have in a vs match.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly agree with everything you said here. But my points were on the assumption of a total war, and the Technocracy trying to completely wipe the Sabbat. On a case-by-case scenario, most agents of the Union would certainly think the vampires as a first priority. But the Union as a whole, and the Sabbat as a whole, operate in a other level. The Sabbat as a whole is hard to completely obliterate, even if far weaker than the Technocracy (it is arguable, but not necessarily untrue that they are. It is completely a matter of interpretation), and that would require resources the Union do not have to spare that way. Also, the consequences would harm the Consensus more probably than not, and to the Union as a whole it matters far more. Most single agents, though, are likely to go for the vampires and even ally with some Traditionalists to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157174#post1157174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And since the Revised is not correlated with V20 in any way, so-called &quot;crossover sensibilities&quot; is no excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Your questions is based on a cross-over assumption. Without cross-over, there is no Sabbat for the Union to deal with. And if there is now, it is probably a recent find and have nothing necessarily to do with the Sabbat described elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157354#post1157354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have already done it in my campaign, so don't worry; vampires are not gone completely extinct yet, but they are mostly eradicated and an nuisance at the worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is exactly how it worked for Mage until M20. Not being bent on cross-over, on Mage the vampires and other night-folk are near extinct nuisances. I want to make it clear that I only argued against the notion of complete extermination, and assuming cross-over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T12:38:53-08:00","id":1157613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157354#post1157354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have already done it in my campaign, so don't worry; vampires are not gone completely extinct yet, but they are mostly eradicated and an nuisance at the worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Hope you had a good time. So why are you <i>still</i> on this screed?. You don't need anyone's permission. You've already decided that's how your Mage world works and you've put it into practice at your table. What purpose is served by continuing to insist upon and trying to justify your weird, kind of bullying obsession with belittling another game line and talking up a power fantasy of dominating and eradicating its denizens? <br /> <br /> It's a little creepy. I'm asking you to chill. Please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T15:34:43-08:00","id":1157648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157613#post1157613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What purpose is served by continuing to insist upon and trying to justify your weird, kind of bullying obsession with belittling another game line</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Since I cannot comprehend how the inhuman monsters likes of Sabbat could coexist with the Union in the Mage. If you think it is an obsession, call it a <i>purifying </i>obsession. Nor I belittle another game line. I'm </span></span></span>denunciating <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">an affront to humankind. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157613#post1157613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and talking up a power fantasy of dominating and eradicating its denizens?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm <i>genuinely </i>offended. You are belittling and insulting me. Besides, how can you not only condone, but </span></span></span>sympathize<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, advocate and justify the continued existence of the likes of Sabbat and Giovanni? Are you not a human being? </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157613#post1157613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little creepy. I'm asking you to chill. Please.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems you are a little agitated. Why are you so upset with me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-10-2017, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T08:30:53-08:00","id":1157759,"title":"","content":"Ok, calm down you two, stop taking this game too personally. It is just a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157648#post1157648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Since I cannot comprehend how the inhuman monsters likes of Sabbat could coexist with the Union in the Mage. If you think it is an obsession, call it a <i>purifying </i>obsession. Nor I belittle another game line. I'm </span></span></span>denunciating <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">an affront to humankind. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>From an in-setting standpoint, I think it fairly valid to want to cleanse the world from such a terrorizing group of bestial monstrosities without almost any redeeming quality. But from an OoC view, to call down an entire game line and state that your favored group simply could do it certainly seems more than a little bullying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157648#post1157648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm <i>genuinely </i>offended. You are belittling and insulting me. Besides, how can you not only condone, but </span></span></span>sympathize<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, advocate and justify the continued existence of the likes of Sabbat and Giovanni? Are you not a human being? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>He isn't sympathizing with the Sabbat and Giovanni. They don't exist. As the Technocracy don't exist. Neither do vampires, mages or werebeasts. There is a lot of distinction between saying that a given fictional group can or can not do something to another fictional group, and saying that they deserve or not, or that they have a right to something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157648#post1157648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems you are a little agitated. Why are you so upset with me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you stepped in his toes as much as he stepped on yours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1157613#post1157613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. Hope you had a good time. So why are you <i>still</i> on this screed?. You don't need anyone's permission. You've already decided that's how your Mage world works and you've put it into practice at your table. What purpose is served by continuing to insist upon and trying to justify your weird, kind of bullying obsession with belittling another game line and talking up a power fantasy of dominating and eradicating its denizens?<br /> <br /> It's a little creepy. I'm asking you to chill. Please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chill out too, guy. If you can't withstand his opinion, you don't have to read it. I know what you're feeling, but you shouldn't be taking this so personal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T16:22:13-08:00","id":1158014,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">From an in-setting standpoint, I think it fairly valid to want to cleanse the world from such a terrorizing group of bestial monstrosities without almost any redeeming quality. But from an OoC view, to call down an entire game line and state that your favored group simply could do it certainly seems more than a little bullying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, if the Technocracy could just annihilate their enemies then there wouldn't be a game to play. That's why they didn't manage to eradicate the Traditions (it wasn't from a lack of <i>trying</i>). If being a Technocrat meant to have a &quot;call the reinforces, you win&quot; app in your cell phone, they wouldn't be fun to play as there would be no challenge.<br /> <br /> The show has to go on, if Crossover was a bigger thing and each splat counted as more than a small note in the antagonist section, then I think that the Sabbat would be more than fitting antagonists for the Technocracy. But then one would want the Sabbat to rise up the chalenge in order to have interesting stories for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-12-2017, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T17:36:36-08:00","id":1158033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm <i>genuinely </i>offended. You are belittling and insulting me. Besides, how can you not only condone, but </span></span></span>sympathize<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, advocate and justify the continued existence of the likes of Sabbat and Giovanni? Are you not a human being? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yo, what's next? saying that D&amp;D players that want to play evil alignaments are <i>monsters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i> .<br /> <br /> Something I always say it's that WoD games weren't built with the other games in mind, things are bound to not make a lot of sense, contradictions abound. There's a lot of people that say Vampire and the Technocracy can't coexist in a setting - that's not to say that it can't be explained but you would have to do some concessions that not everyone wants to make. I totally understand, as I have been piss off by similar stuff before<br /> <br /> We've given you the canon answer and a few ideas of how to make it have sense, obviously they weren't to your satisfaction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. Hope you had a good time. So why are you <i>still</i> on this screed?. You don't need anyone's permission. You've already decided that's how your Mage world works and you've put it into practice at your table. What purpose is served by continuing to insist upon and trying to justify your weird, kind of bullying obsession with belittling another game line and talking up a power fantasy of dominating and eradicating its denizens?<br /> <br /> It's a little creepy. I'm asking you to chill. Please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, people in these forums seem to believe that the canon of this game it's important or something.<br /> <br /> Let the one that has never been involved on a &quot;splat vs splat&quot; cast the first stone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T18:01:10-08:00","id":1158304,"title":"","content":"As much as cannon isn't sacred on most of our games, it is still the only semblance of a common ground we have to develop any discussion.<br /> <br /> By the way, it could be a valid idea, in a cross-over presumption, to really make the Sabbat the biggest threat and downplay the war with the Traditions. I already had Technocracy games focused on fighting threats from other splats, and it does play well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T22:38:41-08:00","id":1158361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1158304#post1158304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, it could be a valid idea, in a cross-over presumption, to really make the Sabbat the biggest threat and downplay the war with the Traditions. I already had Technocracy games focused on fighting threats from other splats, and it does play well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think that the Sabbat be the biggest threat in such a crossover, instead of the Camarilla?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T23:32:32-08:00","id":1158373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1158361#post1158361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think that the Sabbat be the biggest threat in such a crossover, instead of the Camarilla?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the biggest threat to the Technocracy from a martial standpoint, but the biggest threats to the Technocracy's <i>interests</i>. Maintaining the Consensus is one of, if not THE, biggest of the Union's interests. The Camarilla plays along with the Consensus - working hard to maintain the Masquerade - while the Sabbat does not (as much). Ergo, the Technocracy pays the Camarilla little to no mind, while the Sabbat is an active thorn in the Union's side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T22:06:06-08:00","id":1158772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1158033#post1158033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, people in these forums seem to believe that the canon of this game it's important or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easy enough to avoid these fights just by pluralizing &quot;canon.&quot; Just takes one letter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T06:03:53-08:00","id":1158908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1158772#post1158772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's easy enough to avoid these fights just by pluralizing &quot;canon.&quot; Just takes one letter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. If the authors decide to follow a line that's what the books are going to say to me, I can refuse to buy the material or create my own, but that's a consequence of outrage, not a way to counter it, more so if I'm a fan of said books.<br /> <br /> I love to see mage in other splat books, and if I think they're misrepresented I can't avoid to fell bad-speaking about &quot;canon(s)&quot; say nothing to me, I can't unsee what I read and even if I could, as monteparnas states, that defines the &quot;common ground&quot; when you speak with other people. You don't get to decide what's canon and what isn't. That's the whole point of canonicity.<br /> <br /> There isn't a canon where vampires are annihilated by the technocracy. There just isn't (and some people seem to think that such a canon would be deeply offensive, I wonder how would they feel about plurals if Posthumanity vision was canonized). Books don't endorse that outcome and thus people thinking that's the natural way things should develop would forever be frustrated when they pick up a new WoD book because they won't be able to not see the vampires there<br /> <br /> You can speak about canon(s) when the canon it's contradictory or diverges from itself, but the way you pretend to use the word just makes no sense to me.<br /> <br /> As I see it, the way to avoid these fights it's to have self control and maturity. And nobody I know truly keeps their jimmies unrustled forever, not even you, so learning to forgive it's also a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-15-2017, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T15:04:28-08:00","id":1159211,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> When I say canons I am not talking about individual interpretations. I am talking about the fact that each gameline has its own canon and attempts at reconciling them are often problematic. I'm not saying people shouldn't try to reconcile them. But it should be acknowledged that it's really hard.<br /> <br /> I agree that forgiveness is good, and that I am not exactly an exemplar of neutrality and restraint myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 11-15-2017, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T07:46:42-08:00","id":1159413,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1503_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1503\" data-vbnamecard=\"1503\">Faradn</a> Ho, I totally misinterpreted you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Then I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T11:15:24-08:00","id":1159491,"title":"","content":"It's ok, I probably should have been more clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T10:10:10-08:00","id":1160244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1158361#post1158361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think that the Sabbat be the biggest threat in such a crossover, instead of the Camarilla?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just 'cause that's the theme of the conversation by now, I think. Certainly it could be several other ways around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1151253-questions-about-union-policy?p=1159211#post1159211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> When I say canons I am not talking about individual interpretations. I am talking about the fact that each gameline has its own canon and attempts at reconciling them are often problematic. I'm not saying people shouldn't try to reconcile them. But it should be acknowledged that it's really hard.<br /> <br /> I agree that forgiveness is good, and that I am not exactly an exemplar of neutrality and restraint myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as you're right in the setting having &quot;canons&quot; due to several divergences between game lines, it only goes so far. In the present question, it stands that the Union didn't decimated the Sabbat at absolutely no game line, ever. And that Mage have too little information on them for the possibility being considered without going in the thorny realm of Cross-Over-Schizophrenic-Canon of sorts.<br /> \u200b<br /> That's why the fights are sometimes inevitable. The setting &quot;urge&quot; some considerations that can only be made taking into account contradictory versions, and the need for a common ground makes canon a necessity even when there is not a real one. But with maturity, politeness, and eventual forgiveness, we can and do have a lot of fun with those &quot;fights&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}